                "quoted_status_profile_username": null,
                "reply_count": 20,
                "retweet_count": 1,
                "source": "Twitter for iPhone",
                "text": "Congress has known for months that government funding would run out on September 30th and that the ACA tax credits would expire on January 1st. But rather than bringing us together to negotiate a bipartisan budget bill and to address this health care crisis, in the past 100 days, Speaker Johnson has only called us into Congress 19 of them. The American people, including many federal employees, are working day after day throughout this shutdown \u2013 the least we can do is be in Washington doing the jobs our constituents elected us to do.",
                "text_lang": "en",
